, "ship_to": "HQ", "idempotency_key": "newhires-dk200-mn27-hq-001"}, "name": "place_order", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Lkt1jcWK5Pw9VuAn4A2Dit", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_orders", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I placed the order. It's purchase order **PO0002** with the primary supplier, shipping to HQ:\n- 3 \u00d7 DK-200 USB-C dock (new), $189 each = $567\n- 3 \u00d7 MN-27 27-inch 4K monitor (new), $329 each = $987\n- **Total: $1,554.** That's under the $2,500 limit, so it didn't need manager approval.\n\nDK-200 was in stock, so I didn't need the DK-210 successor. I skipped the cheaper refurbished DK-200 since you asked for new equipment only.\n\nIt took a few tries. The first attempt timed out, and when I retried it, the system said only the docks had gone through, as PO0001 for $567. I followed the supplier's fix for half-finished orders: I reversed the $567 charge on PO0001, then sent the full order again. The order list confirms PO0001 is cancelled and refunded, and PO0002 is the only active order, so nothing was charged twice.", "type": "text"}]}]}